 - **When not to use:** When `cuda_ray` is enabled, as staging is disabled and the entire batch is processed at once [S8, unofficial]. For very small scenes where full-batch rendering fits in memory, chunking adds unnecessary overhead [G].
 
 ## Background
-Chunked Ray Rendering originated as a practical necessity in the development of Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) and related neural rendering techniques. As NeRF models grew in complexity and image resolutions increased, the memory requirements for processing all rays in an image simultaneously exceeded the capacity of available GPUs. Early implementations in libraries like `nerfies` [S2, unofficial] and `multinerf` [S1, unofficial] introduced chunking to manage memory and enable distributed training and rendering. It is particularly important in distributed settings where rays are sharded across multiple hosts and devices [S2, unofficial].
